    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite passes: **46 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**, including the new `Cp33Tests` and all previously existing tests.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the specification change in `POST /api/owners` (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`): a supplied `registrationDate` later than the server date is now rejected with HTTP 400.\n\nThe added check, placed just before the effective-date/business-day computation:\n\n```java\nif (owner.getRegistrationDate() != null && owner.getRegistrationDate().isAfter(LocalDate.now())) {\n    return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);\n}\n```\n\nKey points:\n- It validates the **supplied** date (from the request body, mapped onto the owner) against `LocalDate.now()` \u2014 the server date \u2014 *before* the existing business-day rolling logic, so a future date can't be \"corrected\" into acceptance.\n- `null` (no date supplied) is left alone, preserving the existing default-to-today behavior. `Cp07` (explicit past dates + weekend rolling), `Cp20` (default weekday), `Cp14`/`Cp21` (membership/customer code) all still pass.\n- The new `Cp33Tests.errorRejectsFutureDate` (posting `registrationDate: \"2999-01-01\"`) now returns 400 as required.",
